From df17e877a507c88b0218c7acf4605b590ce3814d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 11:26:09 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] HTDESIGNER-64: design mode shows everything, Visible decides
 at run time (0.64.0)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun (the Above9050 screenshot): "我需要向WPF一樣 所有東西都顯示在上面 / 並且屬性可以
設定要不要隱藏 / 當軟體啟動時才判定隱藏還是顯示 / 編輯的時候我需要全部都顯示不要隱藏".
Like the BCB6 / WinForms form designer:
- DESIGN mode draws every component and every tab whatever hides it when the
  page runs: Visible=False (display:none in its style, 71 on HW.IoSetView),
  a machine's "-only" rule (the golden Stack tabs on a 9050, Above9050
  elsewhere), an option rule (rule-hide), the page's JS. How: the page's own
  <style> rules that hide only components are switched off while designing
  (not menus / popups), each component still hidden gets data-htd-show="<its
  own display>" (read with the display:none taken out, the style attribute
  put back as it was) -- the source is never touched. A tab sheet's body
  still follows its tab; what the user hid with the eye stays hidden. The
  page's later hiding is caught by a MutationObserver (inside the form only).
- OPERATE mode = as the page runs (rules back, marks gone).
- Visible in the properties panel = the element's own display:none (not
  "is it drawn now"): off writes display:none, the component keeps showing
  while designing, the panel says 執行時隱藏；設計時照樣顯示 (or 執行時由頁面決定
  for a machine / option rule). The component tree marks 執行時隱藏 (tree row
  field 8).

Tests (all 4 layers pass: lib 142, smoke 145, real VS Code 136): probe (the
real HW.IoSetView: design = all 5 Stack 1 tabs + grpLoaderFunc marked, its
style untouched; operate = only Above9050 on the 9050 / 4 tabs without, the
group hidden; Visible off = display:none written and still shown, on again =
taken out), smoke (the tree's 執行時隱藏), real VS Code (grpLoaderFunc marked
in the tree).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
